    "text": "96\n\n Selling Your Business? Keep Diligence From Killing Your Deal\nHi Sara,\nThinking about selling your business? Buckle up \u2013 because the diligence process is where deals are made\u2026or broken.\nBut don\u2019t worry, I\u2019m here to break it down into real talk \u2013 no corporate jargon, no stress headaches (well, fewer of those, anyway).\nStep1: Sign That NDA \u2013 Seriously\nBefore you share anything, get an NDA in place. That client list you built with sweat and caffeine? You don\u2019t want it floating around. Protect it.\nStep 2: The Buyer\u2019s Checklist \u2013 AKA, Your New Homework\nOnce you find a buyer, they\u2019ll hand you a checklist that looks like it was written by someone with a PhD in Overwhelming You. Don\u2019t freak out. It\u2019s a catch-all list. Some stuff won\u2019t apply to you. Drop \u201cn/a\u201d on the things that don\u2019t apply like environmental concerns and tackle the rest. Completing the checklist should be a collaborative process, so delegate everything to the Buyer where you can. Weekly calls can help keep momentum.\nStep 3: The Virtual Data Room \u2013 Less of a Vault, More of a Beat Up Filing Cabinet\nUpload your docs to a Virtual Data Room (VDR). Think of it as a digital safe deposit box for your business secrets. This is what the buyer will comb through to build the purchase agreement later.\nStep 4: The Purchase Agreement \u2013 Your Business, in Legalese\nEverything you upload becomes part of this holy grail document \u2013 complete with \u201cschedules\u201d (fancy term for all the details). This is what locks in the deal. The Schedules are very protective for you, you want to add as much detail as you can to them. This is the one easy thing too many sellers leave on the table.\nPro Tip: Keep Your Golden Goose Safe\nYour client list? That\u2019s your crown jewel. Don\u2019t hand it over until the deal is signed, sealed, and delivered. No early peeks.\nDeals Fall Through \u2013 Stay Ready\nNot every deal closes. Keep your data room organized and maintain a good copy so you\u2019re prepped for the next buyer if needed. I promise the second round is easier!\nCall in the Pros (That\u2019s What We\u2019re Here For)\nLean on your lawyer and other experts to avoid expensive mistakes. You don\u2019t want to be the person who sells their business only to get sued when you were supposed to be sailing off into the sunset.\nSelling your business is a long elaborate process. It\u2019s part paperwork, part poker face, and a lot of \u201cWhy is this checklist so long?\u201d But with the right team and the right prep, you\u2019ll get to that smooth transition \u2013 and maybe even a celebratory drink after.\nGot questions? Thinking about selling? Check out our courses here on Deal Academy to help you get started. \nTo smarter deals,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nBusiness Consultant and Founder of Deal Academy\nP.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and want me to keep an eye out for you, fill out this form here.\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers podcast episodes by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
