order=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"vertical-align:top;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;\">\n              \n    <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"\" width=\"100%\">\n          <tbody>\n            <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <p style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:100%;\">\n      </p>\n      \n      <!--[if mso | IE]><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:520px;\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"520px\" ><tr><td style=\"height:0;line-height:0;\"> &nbsp;\n</td></tr></table><![endif]-->\n    \n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr><tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><h2 style=\"margin-top: 14pt;margin-bottom: 4pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Selling Your Business? Keep Diligence From Killing Your Deal</span></h2><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Hi Sara,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Thinking about selling your business? Buckle up \u2013 because the diligence process is where deals are made\u2026or broken.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">But don\u2019t worry, I\u2019m here to break it down into real talk \u2013 no corporate jargon, no stress headaches (well, fewer of those, anyway).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>Step1: Sign That NDA \u2013 Seriously<br></strong>Before you share anything, get an NDA in place. That client list you built with sweat and caffeine? You don\u2019t want it floating around. Protect it.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>Step 2: The Buyer\u2019s Checklist \u2013 AKA, Your New Homework<br></strong>Once you find a buyer, they\u2019ll hand you a checklist that looks like it was written by someone with a PhD in Overwhelming You. Don\u2019t freak out. It\u2019s a catch-all list. Some stuff won\u2019t apply to you. Drop \u201cn/a\u201d on the things that don\u2019t apply like environmental concerns and tackle the rest. Completing the checklist should be a collaborative process, so delegate everything to the Buyer where you can. Weekly calls can help keep momentum.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>Step 3: The Virtual Data Room \u2013 Less of a Vault, More of a Beat Up Filing Cabinet<br></strong>Upload your docs to a Virtual Data Room (VDR). Think of it as a digital safe deposit box for your business secrets. This is what the buyer will comb through to build the purchase agreement later.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>Step 4: The Purchase Agreement \u2013 Your Business, in Legalese<br></strong>Everything you upload becomes part of this holy grail document \u2013 complete with \u201cschedules\u201d (fancy term for all the details). This is what locks in the deal. The Schedules are very protective for you, you want to add as much detail as you can to them. This is the one easy thing too many sellers leave on the table.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>Pro Tip: Keep Your Golden Goose Safe<br></strong>Your client list? That\u2019s your crown jewel. Don\u2019t hand it over until the deal is signed, sealed, and delivered. No early peeks.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>Deals Fall Through \u2013 Stay Ready<br></strong>Not every deal closes. Keep your data room organized and maintain a good copy so you\u2019re prepped for the next buyer if needed. I promise the second round is easier!</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"><strong>Call in the Pros (That\u2019s What We\u2019re Here For)<br></strong>Lean on your lawyer and other experts to avoid expensive mistakes. You don\u2019t want to be the person who sells their business only to get sued when you were supposed to be sailing off into the sunset.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Selling your business is a long elaborate process. It\u2019s part paperwork, part poker face, and a lot of \u201cWhy is this checklist so long?\u201d But with the right team and the right prep, you\u2019ll get to that smooth transition \u2013 and maybe even a celebratory drink after.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Got questions? Thinking about selling? </span><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/257eba14abe?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px; color: #3425db !important\">Check out our courses here on Deal Academy to help you get started. </span></a></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px; color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">To smarter deals,<br>Sara Sharp<br>Partner, SK&amp;S Law Group<br>Business Consultant and Founder of Deal Academy</span></p><p><strong><em>P.S. If you're looking to buy or sell an accounting firm, and